<title>DENMARK: Bang &amp; Olufsen 6-mo 1996/97 profit climbs.</title>
<headline>Bang &amp; Olufsen 6-mo 1996/97 profit climbs.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Nov 30, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Pre-tax result before minorities  174 vs 132</p>
<p> Group net turnover		  1,550 vs 1,335</p>
<p> Group operating result		174 vs 128</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Danish audio/video/television maker is Bang &amp; Olufsen Holding A/S, which is 25 percent owned by Netherlands-based Philips Electronics NV. It said in a statement that it expected full year 1996/97 pre-tax and minorities profits of around 325 million crowns, against 1995/96's 272 million crowns.  </p>
<p>The result was above average analyst expectations of a 166 million crown pre-tax and extraordinary items interim profit.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom, 45-33-969650</p>
</text>
